.TH LOGGER 1 "2026-05-02" "4.3" "Logger Library Manual"
.SH NAME
logger \- lightweight asynchronous thread-safe C logging library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #define LOGGER_IMPLEMENTATION
.B #include "logger.h"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Logger
is an asynchronous, lock-free, thread-safe single-header logging library written in C.
 It supports POSIX, Windows and Apple platforms and requires minimum C11 or C++17.
.PP
 The library follows the STB-style single-header pattern: define
.B LOGGER_IMPLEMENTATION
in exactly one translation unit before including the header.
 To build a shared object instead, define both
.B LOGGER_IMPLEMENTATION
and
.B LOGGER_BUILD
during compilation.
.SH QUICK START
.nf
#define LOGGER_IMPLEMENTATION
#include "logger.h"

int main(void) {
    Logger *lg = lg_alloc();
    LoggerConfig cfg = LOGGER_CONFIG_DEFAULTS();
    lg_append_sink(&cfg, stdout, LG_OUT_TTY);
    lg_init(lg, "logs", cfg);

    lg_info("Hello, %s!", "world");

    lg_destroy(lg);
    lg_free(lg);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH LIFECYCLE FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR "int lg_init" "(Logger *instance, const char *logs_dir, LoggerConfig config)"
 Main initializer. Creates the writer thread and sets up sinks.
 Returns 1 on success.
 Dead instances can be re-initialized with this function.
 Automatically sets the active instance if none is set.
.TP
.BR "int lg_init_defaults" "(Logger *instance, const char *logs_dir)"
 Initializer with default configuration. Equivalent to calling
.B lg_init
with
.BR LOGGER_CONFIG_DEFAULTS() .
.TP
.BR "int lg_init_opt" "(Logger *instance, const char *logs_dir, ...)"
 Initializer with optional named parameters (C99 only, unavailable in C++ and LOGGER_BUILD).
 Accepts dot-notation overrides:
.BR "lg_init_opt(lg, \(dqlogs\(dq, .localTime=0)" .
.TP
.BR "int lg_init_flat" "(Logger *inst, const char *logs_dir, int local_time, int max_log_files, int generateDefaultFile, LgSinks sinks, LgLogPolicy log_policy, log_formatter_t log_formatter)"
Flat (struct-free) version of
.BR lg_init .
Intended for FFI consumers whose language cannot construct C structs.
.TP
.BR "int lg_destroy" "(Logger *instance)"
 Shuts down the writer thread, flushes remaining messages and clears instance fields.
 Returns 1 on success.
.B Does not free memory.
Pass NULL to destroy the active instance.
.B Warning:
 calling destroy while producer threads are still active causes undefined behaviour.
 Ensure all producers have finished before calling this.
.TP
.BR "Logger* lg_alloc" "(void)"
Heap-allocates and zero-initialises a Logger instance. Use with
.BR lg_free .
.TP
.BR "void lg_free" "(Logger *inst)"
Frees a heap-allocated Logger instance. Call only after
.BR lg_destroy .
.SH ACTIVE INSTANCE
.TP
.BR "int lg_set_active_instance" "(Logger *inst)"
Sets the global active instance used by implicit-instance log functions.
.TP
.BR "Logger* lg_get_active_instance" "(void)"
Returns the current active instance.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS LoggerConfig struct
.nf
typedef struct {
    int           localTime;          /* default: 1 (true)  */
    int           maxFiles;           /* default: 0         */
    int           generateDefaultFile;/* default: 1 (true)  */
    LgSinks       sinks;              /* default: empty     */
    LgLogPolicy   logPolicy;          /* default: LG_DROP   */
    log_formatter_t logFormatter;     /* default: NULL      */
} LoggerConfig;
.fi
.TP
.BR "LoggerConfig LOGGER_CONFIG_DEFAULTS" "(...)"
 Returns a LoggerConfig populated with the defaults shown above.
 In C99 and later, fields can be overridden via variadic arguments.
 Not available for override in C++ or below C99.
.TP
.BR "LoggerConfig lg_config_defaults" "(void)"
 Function wrapper for
.BR LOGGER_CONFIG_DEFAULTS() .
 Useful in FFI contexts where macros are unavailable.
.TP
.BR "int lg_append_sink" "(LoggerConfig *config, FILE *f, LgOutType type)"
 Appends a file sink to the config. Up to 8 sinks are supported.
.I type
is one of
.BR LG_OUT_TTY ", " LG_OUT_FILE " or " LG_OUT_NET .
.SH LOG POLICIES
.TP
.B LG_DROP
If the ring buffer is full, the incoming log message is silently discarded. (default)
.TP
.B LG_BLOCK
Producer adaptively waits until space is available in the ring buffer.
.TP
.B LG_PRIORITY_BASED
Priority-based eviction policy.
